Greetings,

 due to a variety of dissatisfactions with the mailing list service at
 sourceforge (spam problems, inconvenient auto-unsubscription) the
 list 
    nfs@lists.sourceforge.net
 is being discontinued.
 The list linux-nfs@vger.kernel.org has been created to replace it.

 What you should do:

  1/ subscribe to linux-nfs@vger.kernel.org

    See linux-nfs@vger.kernel.org  for details

  2/ unsubscribe from nfs@lists.sourceforge.net

      You can do this from this page:

        https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/nfs

  All mail to nfs@lists.sourceforge.net will before forwarded to
  linux-nfs for at least the rest of this year (but probably not much
  beyond that).  So you won't miss anything.

  I have asked for MARC and GMANE to subscribe to the new list.  If
  you have another favourite mail archive, you might like to ask them
  to subscribe to the new list too.


 Further subscription to nfs@lists.sourceforge.net will not be
 accepted.

 I suspect that the only dissatisfaction that people might have with
 the vger list is that you won't get '[NFS]' in the subject.  Most
 mail readers should be able to filter on the 'to' header so that you
 don't need to visually filter on the 'subject' header.  I'm sure that
 if it is really an issue, someone will post a clever procmail rule
 which puts the '[NFS]' back :-)

I hope this will not inconvenience anyone.

In case any one is interested, there are currently 638 addresses
subscribed to nfs@lists.sourceforge.net.  Let's see if we can make it
below 300 by December :-)
Similarly there are currently 21 subscriptions to linux-nfs. Can we
make it 100 by next week?

NeilBrown

